**Organizational behaviour (OB)** is described on the slides in several ways:

- how individuals interact within groups;
- the study of **human behavior in the organization**;
- the application of **psychology in the workplace**;
- how people and groups in organizations behave;
- the role of organizational **systems, structures and processes** in shaping behavior, to understand how organizations really work.

The formal version: OB studies **the influence that individuals, groups and structure have on behavior within organizations**.

**Stephen P Robbins:** *"Organisational Behaviour is a systematic study of the actions and attitudes that people exhibit within the organisations."*
